From 5a4699f5739513f54c01fb8d152c5ad59dce33f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Needham <06needhamt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:15:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avformat: add HD DVD demuxer using libhddvd

Demuxes a title of an HD DVD disc, in the manner of the dvdvideo demuxer:
libhddvd lists the disc's titles (Standard Content titles from its title
table, Advanced Content titles from its playlist) with their chapters, and
reads a title's cells or clips from the disc's EVO files as one MPEG
program stream, which a nested MPEG-PS demuxer parses. The PS demuxer
already knows the EVO substreams (AC-3/E-AC-3, DTS-HD, LPCM, MLP, VC-1).

The sub-demuxer is restarted where the title's data jumps from one cell or
clip to one that does not follow it on the disc. Each extent's timestamps
are moved onto the title's time: by the title's time maps for Advanced
Content, whose clips can start inside an EVOBU, or else by the first video
timestamp at the extent's start, as Standard Content cells start on the
frame they play first. Timestamps so stay continuous across joins, chapter
ranges and seeks. Chapters are exported, and audio and subtitle streams take their
language from the title set's stream attributes or the playlist's tracks.

Options: title (default: the longest title), chapter_start and
chapter_end. libhddvd (LGPL 2.1 or later) does not decrypt AACS: a
protected sector ends demuxing with an error. Menus and angles are not
supported.
