+@section hddvd
+
+HD DVD demuxer, powered by libhddvd.
+
+Demuxes a title of an HD DVD disc: a Standard Content title from the disc's
+title table (@file{HVDVD_TS/HV000I01.IFO}), or an Advanced Content title from
+its playlist (the highest-numbered @file{ADV_OBJ/VPLSTnnn.XPL}). libhddvd
+reads the title's cells or clips from the disc's EVO files as one MPEG program
+stream, which the MPEG-PS demuxer parses. Timestamps follow the title's own
+time, across the joins between cells or clips. The title's chapters are
+exported, and audio and subtitle streams get their language from the title
+set's stream attributes (Standard Content) or from the playlist's tracks
+(Advanced Content, where a track's @code{streamNumber} is taken to name the
+substream: unconfirmed on a disc).
+
+The input is the directory of a mounted disc, or of a copy of the disc's
+files; ISO images and drives are not read directly.
+Activate with @code{-f hddvd} in front of the input.
+
+This demuxer does NOT decrypt anything, and neither does libhddvd: a title
+protected by AACS fails to read when the first protected sector is reached.
+Menus, interactive Advanced Content applications, angles and secondary
+(picture-in-picture) streams are not supported.
+
+FFmpeg must be built with the configure switch @code{--enable-libhddvd}.
+
+@subsection Options
+
+@table @option
+
+@item title @var{int}
+The title number to demux, counted from 1 in the disc's title table or in
+its playlist. Advanced Content titles that play no audio or video (e.g. a
+title that only runs a menu application) cannot be chosen.
+Default is 0, the longest title with audio or video.
+
+@item chapter_start @var{int}
+The chapter to start demuxing from. Timestamps then start at the chapter's
+start. Default is 1, the first chapter.
+
+@item chapter_end @var{int}
+The last chapter to demux, inclusive. Default is 0, the title's last chapter.
+
+@end table
+
+Seeking is supported. It estimates the position within a cell or clip from
+its duration and reads from about a second before the requested time.
+
+@subsection Examples
+
+@itemize
+@item
+Remux the longest title of a disc copied to @file{/media/disc}, with its
+chapters:
+@example
+ffmpeg -f hddvd -i /media/disc -map 0 -c copy out.mkv
+@end example
+
+@item
+Demux chapters 3 to 6 of title 2:
+@example
+ffmpeg -f hddvd -title 2 -chapter_start 3 -chapter_end 6 -i /media/disc ...
+@end example
+@end itemize
+
 @section hls
 
 HLS demuxer
